8	// This file guards the reorg rule that a hash living inside the replaced
9	// suffix may be reused by the alternate branch — including at a DIFFERENT
10	// height than it used to occupy. TestReorgRemovedSuffixHashesMayReappear
11	// already covers reuse at the original height; here the reused hashes move,
12	// so every lookup that resolves a hash must follow its new position:
13	//
